            <ArticleTitle>Pain on injection of propofol: comparison of lignocaine with metoclopramide.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>316-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We have conducted a randomized, double-blind study in 255 ASA I and II patients to compare the efficacy of lignocaine and metoclopramide in minimizing the pain of injection of i.v. propofol. When administered immediately before propofol into a dorsal hand vein, compared with placebo both drugs significantly reduced the incidence of pain on subsequent injection of propofol (P &lt; 0.001). Twenty patients who had received metoclopramide (n = 85) experienced pain, compared with 18 who had received lignocaine (n = 85) and 42 who had been pretreated with saline (n = 85).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
